title: Example - Markdown horizontal rule
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Markdown

A line consisting of 3 or more matching `-`, `*`, or `_` characters (additional characters may have whitespace between them, trailing whitespace OK) renders as `<hr>`. Up to 3 leading spaces is allowed; 4 or more is treated as indented code in CommonMark. Shipped as three `kind: hr` markers: [vocab/markdown/HR-DASH](#vocab/markdown/HR-DASH), [vocab/markdown/HR-STAR](#vocab/markdown/HR-STAR), [vocab/markdown/HR-UNDER](#vocab/markdown/HR-UNDER).

